-- Lesson 1: What is a Percentage?
'{"hook":"When Roman tax collectors needed to take a fair share from every merchant — whether they earned 50 coins or 5000 — they invented a system based on hundreds. We still use it every day: percentages.","inventor":{"name":"Roman Tax System","birth_year":null,"death_year":null,"nationality":"Roman","bio":"The concept of percentages emerged from Roman taxation, where taxes were calculated as a fraction of 100. The Latin phrase ''per centum'' (per hundred) became the basis for our modern percentage system."},"year_invented":-100,"etymology":{"word":"percent","from":"Latin","parts":[{"root":"per","meaning":"for each, through"},{"root":"centum","meaning":"hundred"}]},"story_paragraphs":["In ancient Rome, Emperor Augustus levied a tax called centesima rerum venalium — a 1/100 tax on goods sold at auction. This ''one per hundred'' concept was one of the earliest uses of percentage-like thinking.","The idea of expressing parts ''out of 100'' proved incredibly useful because 100 is easy to work with mentally. Whether you''re splitting 50 items or 5 million, ''25 percent'' means the same proportion.","The % symbol itself evolved over centuries. Italian merchants in the 1400s wrote ''per cento'' which was gradually abbreviated. By the 1600s, the modern % symbol appeared — a compact way to write ''divided by 100.''","Today percentages are inescapable: sales tax, battery life, exam scores, weather forecasts (''40% chance of rain''), nutrition labels, interest rates, and statistics. Understanding percentages is understanding the modern world."],"key_contributors":[{"name":"Italian merchants","contribution":"Developed percentage calculations for trade and banking in the 1400s-1500s"},{"name":"Simon Stevin","contribution":"Connected percentages to decimal notation in 1585, making calculations simpler"}],"real_world_applications":[{"name":"Shopping","icon":"🛒","description":"Sales discounts: 20% off means you pay 80% of the original price"},{"name":"Grades","icon":"📝","description":"Test scores are percentages — 45 out of 50 = 90%"},{"name":"Weather","icon":"🌧️","description":"Rain probability: 60% chance of rain means 6 out of 10 similar days would have rain"},{"name":"Finance","icon":"🏦","description":"Interest rates on savings and loans are percentages — 5% annual interest"},{"name":"Health","icon":"❤️","description":"Phone battery (73%), blood oxygen (98%), body fat percentage"}],"image":{"url":null,"alt":"Roman coins showing centesima tax markings","attribution":"Wikimedia Commons, public domain","source_url":null}}'::jsonb)
